# Checkout API (Cursor)

## Read first

- Implementation: `src/`
- HTTP contract: `openapi.yaml`
- Standards: `docs/RULEBOOK.md` (link, do not duplicate wholesale)

## Workflow

Run `npm test` before commit. Keep PRs small. Write commit messages that explain why.

## Context discipline

Prefer `src/` and OpenAPI excerpts. Do not load coverage trees or full CI XML logs into
every agent turn — summarize failures instead.

## Lockfiles

Do not paste `package-lock.json` into chat for routine edits. Use `package.json` and
targeted dependency names.

## Duplication

Search `src/` before adding validators, formatters, or retry helpers.

## Contracts

Update `openapi.yaml` with any public HTTP change.

## Security

No secrets in code or logs. No card data in examples.

## Overlap

These bullets intentionally mirror `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` — TokenForge hybrid scans
should flag redundant always-on instruction stacks.

## Bad habit (intentional fixture)

Some teams ask agents to "always load the entire RULEBOOK into context" — **do not do that
here**; cite sections instead. (Copilot instructions elsewhere may disagree — canonical
source is `AGENTS.md`.)

## Webhooks

Verify signatures on inbound webhook routes when added.

## Pagination

Cursor-based lists only for new endpoints.

## Retries

Use shared helpers under `src/` for outbound HTTP retry.

## Lint and CI

Fix lint before pushing; CI is not a first pass for style fixes.

## Load tests

Keep k6/Locust output out of git.

## Branch hygiene

Delete merged branches promptly.

## Release notes

Note HTTP contract changes in PR descriptions.

